W:1. Come all brother tradesment that travel along
W:O pray, come and tell me where the trade is all gone
W:Long time have I travelled, and I cannot find none
W:
W:[Chorus:]
W:And it's, oh, the hard times of Old England
W:In Old England, very hard times
W:
W:2. Provisions you buy at the shop, it is true
W:But if you've no money, there's none there for you
W:So what's a poor man and his family to do?  [Chorus]
W:
W:3. If you go to the shop and you ask for a job
W:They will answer you there with a shake and a nod
W:So that's enough to make a man turn out and rob  [Chorus]
W:
W:4. You will see the poor tradesmen a-walkin the street
W:From morning to night for employment to seek
W:And scarce have they got any shoes to their feet  [Chorus]
W:
W:5. Our soldiers and sailors have just come from war
W:Been fighting for their Queen and country this year
W:Come home to be starved, better stayed where they were  [Chorus]
W:
W:6. And now to conclude and to finish my song
W:Let us hope that these hard times they will not last long
W:I hope soon to have occasion to alter my song, and it's
W:Oh, the good times of old England
W:In old England, jolly good times!
